grund.toml is read as version 2.

agents-init: An agent entrypoint such as AGENTS.md lacks the grund init block it needs, or carries one this grund does not accept.
broken-stub: A stub's link does not lead to a declaration of its ID.
chapter-cardinality: A declaration has more or fewer chapters of a name than a rule's have sentence allows.
citation-cardinality: A declaration cites a target more or fewer times than a rule allows.
config-multiline-string: A value in a version-2 config holds a multi-line string, which version 2 does not read; it is read for one more release as before, its quotes kept and a line break read as a space.
config-not-toml: A version-2 config holds text TOML refuses, such as a string in an array left open at the end of a line, or a string followed by more text after its closing quote, or a comma before an array's ] with no element before it, which grund still reads for one release.
conflict-marker: A scanned file holds an unresolved merge-conflict block.
dangling: A citation names an ID that no declaration declares.
declaration-near-miss: A heading opens like a declaration, but its ID does not match its kind's ID format.
deprecated-config-location: The config was read from .agents/grund.toml, a location that still works but is deprecated.
discouraged-citation: A citation goes to a target that a should-not entry or rule discourages.
duplicate: The same ID is declared more than once.
duplicate-section: Two section headings in one declaration claim the same section path.
empty-citation-obligation: A must or should citation obligation applies to a kind that has no unit for it to judge.
empty-scan: The scan read no files at all, which usually means its scope is misconfigured.
escaped-citation-resolves: An escaped citation names an ID or section that exists, so it may be a live citation escaped by mistake.
excluded-stub-target: A stub led to a file the scan excludes; that case is now reported as a broken stub.
forbidden-citation: A citation goes to a target that a must-not entry or rule forbids.
front-matter-heading: A heading claims the front-matter field's coordinate in a declaration whose kind reads that field from the file's front matter.
full-scope-ignored: --full was given an explicit path, which it cannot widen, so it changed nothing.
glob-citation: A marked citation is written as a pattern rather than as one ID.
image-index-entry: A citation-only image was all a kind's index held for an ID; such an image is now neither an entry nor an enrollment.
inline-citation-style: A citation's inline note in a code comment breaks the configured note style: too many lines, too wide, the wrong layout, or prose where only the citation is allowed.
invalid-field-value: A field's value is not one of the values its kind admits for it.
invalid-rule: A rule declaration cannot be read: its title, rationale, vocabulary or subject is invalid.
invalid-section-lock: A line of a .grund/sections/ lock file is not an entry grund can read.
invalid-value-binding: A value binding breaks the binding grammar or aims at something it cannot bind.
invalid-value-declaration: A declaration of a kind that holds values is not a valid value.
io: A file or directory could not be read, so the run's view of the tree is incomplete.
local-section-citation: A marker followed by a bare section number is not a citation grund can resolve; write the full ID.
misplaced-declaration: A declaration sits outside the home its kind is configured to live in.
misplaced-field: A field does not stand where its kind places it.
missing-citation: A declaration lacks a citation that a must entry or rule requires.
missing-field: A declaration lacks a field its kind declares.
missing-index-entry: A declaration in a kind's folder is not listed in that folder's index.
missing-section: A citation names a section its declaration does not have.
missing-snapshot: A citation targets a fetched kind whose declarations have not been fetched yet.
mistitled-field: A field's heading is titled differently from the title its kind gives it.
nothing-recognized: The scan read files but recognized no declaration and no citation in them.
optional-member-absent: A workspace member listed as optional is not in this checkout, so it was not read.
orphan-section: A named section path is used before every shorter prefix of it is recorded in the same declaration.
out-of-scope-dangling: Under --full, a file outside the default scope cites an ID that no declaration declares.
out-of-scope-local-section-citation: Under --full, a file outside the default scope writes a marker followed by a bare section number.
out-of-scope-missing-section: Under --full, a file outside the default scope cites a section its declaration does not have.
out-of-scope-shorthand-citation: Under --full, a file outside the default scope writes a number-only shorthand that matches no declaration or several.
out-of-scope-unknown-project: Under --full, a file outside the default scope cites through a project alias the workspace does not know.
oversized-lead: A declaration's lead is longer than the configured word limit.
redundant-config: A directory holds both grund.toml and .agents/grund.toml, and only the first is read.
relative-section-parent: A relative section heading has no parent section one level up for its path to extend.
section-address-changed: A cited section's text has moved to another address, and the cited address now holds something else.
section-heading-level: A section heading's Markdown depth does not match the depth of its section path.
section-outside-declaration: A section heading sits outside every declaration's body.
selected-check-off: A check that --only selected was off for the whole run, so it judged nothing.
shorthand-citation: A number-only shorthand citation is written where the full ID is required, or matches no declaration or several.
shorthand-numeric-run: A number-only shorthand citation is glued to another number, so grund fmt will not expand it.
stub-shape: A heading whose title is one link was read as a stub by one test and as a declaration by another; that can no longer happen.
suggested-citation: A declaration lacks a citation that a should entry or rule suggests.
uncited-unit: A declaration or chapter is cited more or fewer times than a rule's be cited by sentence allows.
undeclared-chapter: A declaration of a closed kind has a chapter that none of the kind's fields declares.
ungrounded: A unit in a place that must be grounded neither cites nor declares an ID.
unknown-project: A citation names a project alias that is not known, or a declaration or section that project does not have.
unlinked-index-entry: An index entry cites a declaration bare rather than as a Markdown link.
unlisted-workspace-block: A directory declares [workspace], but no enclosing workspace lists it among its members.
unmarked-heading: A heading inside a declaration's body is neither a declaration nor a recognized section heading.
unreached-declaration: A declaration lacks the chapter a chapter-scoped citation rule over its kind needs in order to reach it.
unread-scan-root: A file the config names as a scan root is not read, because its name is hidden or its extension is not scanned.
unreadable-front-matter: The front matter of a declaration whose kind declares a front-matter field cannot be read as YAML or TOML keys.
unrecorded-section-citation: A citation names a locked section address that has no entry in the section lock.
unused: A declared ID is never cited.
value-mismatch: A value binding's written value differs from the value its target declares.
yaml-value-source-deferred: A finding that is an error at a YAML value source, or a YAML value source a fetched kind's home skips, is a warning for one release.

Next: grund config explain agents-init
